{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sudsy-unquieting-waxwing","creation_channel":"python","description":"## The gap\n\n`scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` detects raw git mutations by matching CALL NAMES against\n`WRAPPER_NAMES = {\"run_git\", \"run_git_write\", \"_run_git\", \"_git\"}` plus `subprocess` funcs. That\nmatch is on the bare callable name, so a call written as `core._git(\"commit\", ...)` — an\nATTRIBUTE on a module object passed in as a parameter — is invisible to it.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py` uses exactly that shape (`core._git(` at\nline 116, documented as deliberate in its §\"The `core` parameter\" docstring) and carries **zero**\n`# raw-git-ok:` markers, while the sibling functions in `_ref_lock.py` that call bare `_git(...)`\ndo carry them. The lint passes on both — it simply never saw the `_ref_lock_push.py` calls.\n\nThe late-binding `core`-passing pattern is the CORRECT remedy for splitting a module whose git\nprimitive is monkeypatched (it is what keeps `monkeypatch.setattr(mod, \"_git\", ...)` working\nacross a module boundary), so this blind spot widens every time that pattern is used to buy\nmodule-size headroom — including `_store/push_recovery.py` under\n`cinderlike-lucky-akitainu`.\n\n## Why this is a record, not an emergency\n\nThe lint is an advisory guard against ad-hoc raw git in the tracker, not a correctness gate, and\nthe calls it misses are inside modules whose parents already carry the markers. Filed so the\ngap is measured rather than rediscovered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `check_raw_git_writes.py` resolves attribute-form calls whose attribute name is in\n      `WRAPPER_NAMES` (e.g. `core._git(...)`, `mod.run_git(...)`), or the decision not to is\n      recorded with a reason.\n- [ ] `_ref_lock_push.py` and any `push_recovery.py` git call sites are either flagged and\n      marked, or explicitly dispositioned.\n- [ ] A test pins the attribute-form detection so the gap cannot silently reopen.\n","id":"4073-9d4f-c644-44a9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"check_raw_git_writes misses attribute-form git wrapper calls"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786652721130645001,"uuid":"3471d361-aa68-4026-94ea-628d52332e20"}